{"/api/discogs/artist/102898/profile":{"cached":true,"profile":{"id":"102898","image":"https://i.discogs.com/fMK9AciNsrqOewxJjS5yOokM26KpcBrayRaDwurDYzA/rs:fit/g:sm/q:90/h:600/w:476/czM6Ly9kaXNjb2dz/LWRhdGFiYXNlLWlt/YWdlcy9BLTEwMjg5/OC0xMzU0NDA4MDg0/LTQ5MzQuanBlZw.jpeg","imageThumb":"https://i.discogs.com/Gys1J6bNTlVZVcKJReSU4ZoJ7safqXrrAq5DlsIuoz8/rs:fit/g:sm/q:40/h:150/w:150/czM6Ly9kaXNjb2dz/LWRhdGFiYXNlLWlt/YWdlcy9BLTEwMjg5/OC0xMzU0NDA4MDg0/LTQ5MzQuanBlZw.jpeg","profile":"Roger Troutman released music as both Zapp and Roger in the 1980s, attaining success with both, the former being his band and the latter being his solo project with one more album around 1991. Two Warner-released best-of collections compiled his most popular songs from both monikers: \"All The Greatest Hits\" (1993) and \"Greatest Hits, Vol. 2 & More\" (1996). These compilations were released under the artist name Zapp & Roger.","provider":"discogs","ref":"discogs:artist:102898","relations":{"aliases":null,"groups":null,"members":[{"active":true,"id":73142,"name":"Roger Troutman"}],"namevariations":["Roger & Zapp","Roger And Zapp","Roger Troutman & Zapp","Zap/Roger","Zapp","Zapp & Roger Troutman","Zapp & Rogers","Zapp And Roger","Zapp, Roger","Zapp/Roger"]},"schemaVersion":2,"sourceUrl":"https://www.discogs.com/artist/102898-Zapp-Roger","type":"artist","urls":[]}},"/api/discogs/artist/10783/profile":{"cached":true,"profile":{"id":"10783","image":"https://i.discogs.com/OT8iCVzC5GjHIDZZM3zrQJHni499LnhalnwtCDlWab4/rs:fit/g:sm/q:90/h:477/w:466/czM6Ly9kaXNjb2dz/LWRhdGFiYXNlLWlt/YWdlcy9BLTEwNzgz/LTE2MjUzNzYyMDkt/OTIzMi5wbmc.jpeg","imageThumb":"https://i.discogs.com/Yh9mGYFja_DciUISXJ3UT16WXtbchwhQwdtHGNSwOWo/rs:fit/g:sm/q:40/h:150/w:150/czM6Ly9kaXNjb2dz/LWRhdGFiYXNlLWlt/YWdlcy9BLTEwNzgz/LTE2MjUzNzYyMDkt/OTIzMi5wbmc.jpeg","profile":"American hip hop band formed in New York in 1981 as a hardcore punk combo. After the success of their first hip hop track, \"Cooky Puss\" in 1983, they turned into a rap gr