and consolidated the label's operations with that of [l=Elektra Records].\r\n\r\n300 Entertainment is best known for their work with signed and/or managed artists such as [a=Highly Suspect], [a=Coheed And Cambria], [a=Panama (16)], [a=Young Thug (2)], [a=Gunna], [a=Fetty Wap], [a=Cheat Codes] and [a=Megan Thee Stallion].\r\n\r\nAs of 2022, co-founder Kevin Liles, former president of [l=Def Jam Recordings] and EVP of Warner Music, is the chairman and CEO of 300 Elektra Entertainment (3EE), the merger of 300 and Elektra under WMG. Fellow compadre Lyor Cohen, former president of the [l=Island Def Jam Music Group] and CEO of WMG, left the company in 2016 to become head of global music at Google's social video platform, YouTube. Todd Moscowitz, co-founder of 300, EVP of A&R at Def Jam, VP of [l=Asylum]/[l=Warner Records], and general manager of [l=Violator Management], is no longer affiliated as he launched his own music company, [l=Alamo Records (5)], in 2015. Roger Gold, former chairman and CEO of recorded music at WMG and COO of operations at the [l=NFL], has been vice president of 300 Entertainment since its foundation until 2020, when he became SVP of [l=Columbia Records].\r\n","provider":"discogs","ref":"discogs:label:758325","relations":{"parentLabel":{"id":35282,"name":"Elektra Entertainment"},"sublabels":[{"id":1647434,"name":"Dorian Distribution"},{"id":1908105,"name":"FRKST Records"},{"id":19846,"name":"Murder Inc Records"},{"id":1765181,"name":"Unauthorized Entertainment (2)"},{"id":3944637,"name":"Young Stoner Life Records, LLC"}]},"schemaVersion":2,"sourceUrl":"https://www.discogs.com/label/758325-300-Entertainment","type":"label","urls":["http://www.300ent.com","http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/300_Entertainment","http://www.facebook.com/threehundredentertainment","http://www.twitter.com/300","http://www.instagram.com/300ent","http://www.youtube.com/channel/UClO3VS7C-pHAoRh6fYddbLQ"]}},"/api/discogs/release/10003836/credits":{"cached":true,"credits":[{"id":137